manualInstructions.text:
Register the command where you build the application:

  CliApplication.Create(cfg => cfg.AddCommands(new PorticoCommandTool())).Run(args);

Then make the example a test, which is the whole point of declaring it:

  [Fact]
  public void Dispatch_Every_Example()
  {
      var notDispatched = 0;
      new CliContractValidator<IPorticoCommandTool>()
          .Validate(onNotInvoked: (example, reason) => notDispatched++);
      Assert.Equal(0, notDispatched);
  }

Every [CliCommandExample] then runs through the real pipeline, and the test suite goes red
if one stops dispatching.
